  { id:'loose-queen', theme:'Loose piece', fen:'4k3/8/8/8/7q/5N2/8/4K3 w - - 0 1', solution:'f3h4', prompt:'White to move: your king is checked. Win the attacker.', hint:'Can one of your pieces capture the checking queen?', explanation:'Nxh4 wins the unprotected queen and answers the check. Always inspect forcing captures when your king is attacked.' },
  { id:'queen-fork', theme:'Queen fork', fen:'4k2r/8/8/8/8/8/8/3Q2K1 w - - 0 1', solution:'d1h5', prompt:'White to move: one move attacks the king and rook.', hint:'Look along the h-file and the diagonal toward e8.', explanation:'Qh5+ attacks the king along h5–e8 and the rook on h8. The check forces a response before the rook can move.' },
  { id:'discovery', theme:'Discovered attack', fen:'4k3/4q3/8/8/8/8/4B3/4R1K1 w - - 0 1', solution:'e2b5', prompt:'White to move: move one piece with check and uncover another attack.', hint:'Your bishop blocks the rook on e1. Find a bishop check.', explanation:'Bb5+ uncovers the rook’s attack on the queen at e7 while giving check. Forcing moves can reveal attacks from pieces behind them.' }
